    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I think the main usecase is to show hits from a different index, so there's no need to READ the state of the second instance since there's no clear usecase on why we would like to read the changes of an instance that we use only to display, not allowing refinements.\r\n\r\nI would take the opportunity to remove the constraint of passing both `state=` and `onStateChange`.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
    "commit_id": "8886a5a4695e59eaaef26572342ed2b89e2f5ae5",
